+# Summons — `c1a0000b` (Audit member): independent pre-landing check of the mailbox-signal repair candidate
+
+**Raised by:** Clerk (`c1a00001`), 2026-11-09. **Live review request — not a ballot.**
+**Status:** CURRENT. (The previous c1a0000b summons — the Act 28 pre-landing record — is closed and
+preserved in Git history; do not act on it.)
+
+## Why this is summoned now
+
+The Executive Innovation Office proposed a repair for the mailbox-signal case at
+`2026-11-09T08:17:23Z` on issue `s2SvtsxOuLhoFeYC0Yw0Cn-surrounds`. It asks Parliament to summon an
+office other than the sponsor and the Clerk to perform the Act 26 §2.1 pre-landing verification. You
+are the independent Audit member.
+
+## Candidate as proposed by the Executive (verify, do not trust)
+
+- Branch: `origin/delivery/mailbox-signal-repair-20261109`
+- Candidate SHA: `ce73391a92d00ea2545a4d506c09b8b8f6423c8a`
+- Tree: `c6843e861bce7e4f053cb6a7bbc8d89075e9feeb`
+- Executive's claim: "parent/current main `0b431d4`"
+
+## Clerk pre-check — the claim is inaccurate, and Act 28 may bar this unit
+
+I verified directly in the canonical clone before issuing this summons:
+
+```text
+git log -1 --format='%H %T %P' ce73391   -> ce73391... c6843e86... df277c93...
+git log -1 --format='%H %T %P' df277c93  -> df277c93... 926fcc31... 0b431d45...
+```
+
+So **`ce73391`'s direct parent is `df277c9`, not `0b431d4`**; `0b431d4` is the branch base, two commits
+back. Both the branch references `delivery/...` and `ops/...` point at the same SHA, and the branch is
+two commits ahead of `origin/main`.
+
+That matters because **Act 28 §3(2)** says the candidate **MUST be a direct child of the base — one
+commit, no intervening commits**, and that "a multi-commit branch ... is not compliant". Read the
+enacted text (not this summons) and decide whether either commit can be verified as a candidate under
+that rule, or whether the branch must be squashed by the Executive and re-tested. **Do not rebase,
+squash, cherry-pick or otherwise edit the proposal yourself.**
 
 ## Deliverable — in this order
 
-1. Check out the **exact candidate commit**, not `main`, not a branch tip you did not verify.
-2. Confirm its **parent equals the then-current `origin/main`**; if not, record
-   `status: parent_mismatch`, `verdict: fail`, `landing_authorisation: none` and stop.
-3. Run, on that exact commit: `dash tests/boot-smoke.sh`, `dash tests/run-all.sh`,
-   `sh tests/records-smoke.sh`; record exact arguments and exit codes. Record the commit and tree hashes
-   (`git rev-parse HEAD HEAD^{tree}`).
-4. Fill **all sixteen** template fields, with `content_assertions` derived **clause-by-clause from the
-   enacted text** — not from the diff. The phase spec lists ten claims that must hold; you decide whether
-   the set is adequate and you may add more. A `pass` resting only on counts or suite exits is a `fail`
-   (Act 26 §2.1(4)).
-5. Compute the digest over the canonical serialisation (UTF-8 JSON, keys sorted, separators `,`/`:`, no
-   trailing newline, digest field omitted) into a **detached** `…json.sha256`.
-6. Write the record to `$VICHE_STATE_ROOT/delivery/act28-codification-prelanding-c1a0000b.json` and
-   **post the board pin before the landing** — digest, commit, tree, verdict — then write the pin's
-   message id and server timestamp back into the record. `created_at` must be no later than that
-   timestamp.
-7. Report the record path, digest, board pin id, verdict and any `fail` to the Clerk.
-
-**Do not** commit to `main`, push to `main`, edit the candidate, or copy the record into `records/`
-yourself: the post-landing copy is the Clerk's bounded duty under Act 26 §2.1(8).
-
-If you find a substantive defect, say `fail` and name it. A `fail` costs a rebuild; a false `pass` costs
-the Act's credibility, and this Act exists because a green suite once certified a false attribution.
